  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Safeguarding Collective Initiative (Hurras)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">3 implementing organisations (Islamic Relief, Hurras, Basmeh &amp; Zeitooneh) and 2 supporting organisations (CAFOD, Christian Aid) will collaborate to develop a range of products and services to enhance the indigenous approaches to safeguarding within the education sector in Northwest Syria (NWS) Focusing on Children, and to provide a roadmap for international organisations to utilise in future DEC appeals to invest in a decolonial approach to safeguarding by identifying, and investing in the pre-existing indigenous capabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
